    "description": {
      "value": "<div data-ft-phase5-vocab-scrub=\"v1\" style=\"display:none\"></div><p><em>“Yesod fell. The world remembered old names. You answered.”</em></p><p><strong>Oldenborn (Tideborne).</strong> You are a diminished god-fragment, an ancestor-spirit, a genius loci clawing back into embodiment. Folk might call you an elf, a dwarf, a sylph, a goblin—because mortals label what scares them. But you know the truth: you are a place-soul wearing legs.</p><h3>Traits</h3><ul><li><p><strong>Creature Type.</strong> Humanoid (Fey).</p></li><li><p><strong>Size.</strong> Medium.</p></li><li><p><strong>Speed.</strong> 6 squares</p></li><li><p><strong>attributes.</strong> Oldenborn does not grant fixed attribute bonuses; your background handles increases. Your lineage leans toward <strong>SOUL</strong> in fiction and mechanics via Tier powers.</p></li></ul><h3>Oldenborn Core</h3><p>At character creation, you gain <strong>Old Memory, Old Flesh</strong> (Dream-Flesh, Old Paths, Veil-Sight, You Are Remembered).</p><h3>Tideborne Tier Powers</h3><p>You gain your Tier I power at creation, then additional Tier powers as you level (5/11/17). These are granted as features and are intentionally light on automation—Bad Eden loves table truth more than rules-lawyering.</p>",
      "chat": ""
    },
